{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"tenuous-decorative-chimpanzee","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Symptom\n\n`scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py` refused a submit with:\n\n```\nrefusing stale submit: Gerrit reports revision is no longer current\n```\n\non a change whose revision *was* current. Gerrit's own detail endpoint reported\n`current_revision = db3f3e396f1bb50a1350731cba30a6962d44fbaf`, `status: NEW`, two patch sets,\nand that exact SHA as patch set 2 — the same SHA passed to `--revision`.\n\nThe real cause, from the POST body:\n\n```\nCannot rebase db3f3e396f1...: Change 3169 could not be rebased due to a conflict during merge.\n\nmerge conflict(s):\n* docs/release-notes.md\n```\n\n`GET /a/changes/3169/revisions/current/mergeable` confirmed `\"mergeable\": false` under\n`REBASE_IF_NECESSARY`.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py:130-146` wraps the submit POST and maps the whole of HTTP 409\nonto one message:\n\n```python\nexcept urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:\n    if exc.code == 409:\n        print(\n            \"refusing stale submit: Gerrit reports revision is no longer current\",\n            file=sys.stderr,\n        )\n        return 2\n    raise\n```\n\nGerrit returns 409 for several distinct conditions on submit, including an unmergeable change,\nsubmit requirements not satisfied, and a genuinely superseded revision. The handler discards\n`exc.read()` entirely, so the one condition it names is asserted regardless of which occurred.\n\nThe staleness check that *would* be authoritative already ran and passed at `:104-109`, comparing\n`detail[\"current_revision\"]` against `--revision`. So by the time the 409 arrives, staleness has\nbeen ruled out — the message contradicts a check the same script just performed.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe message points the operator at the wrong remedy. \"Revision is no longer current\" means\n*re-inspect votes and re-submit*; a merge conflict means *pre-rebase and resolve*, which is the\ndocumented exception to AGENTS.md's \"do not pre-rebase\" rule. Acting on the printed message\nproduces a loop of re-reading Gerrit state that cannot terminate, because nothing about the\nrevision is wrong. Diagnosis required dropping to a raw authenticated `curl` to read the body\nthe script had already received and thrown away.\n\nThis is also a silent-failure class: any future 409 condition is reported as staleness too.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** The 409 handler reads the response body and includes it in the message, so the\n      printed text names the condition Gerrit reported rather than a fixed guess.\n- [ ] **AC2** When the body indicates the change cannot be merged, the message names the\n      conflict and the remedy (pre-rebase and resolve), not staleness.\n- [ ] **AC3** The script claims staleness only when it can show it — that is, when\n      `current_revision` differs from `--revision`, which is already checked at `:104-109`.\n- [ ] **AC4** A test drives the 409 path with a merge-conflict body and asserts the emitted\n      message contains the conflicting path and does not contain \"no longer current\".\n- [ ] **AC5** A test drives the 409 path with a genuinely superseded revision and asserts the\n      staleness wording is still produced for that case.\n- [ ] **AC6** Exit codes for the distinguished cases are documented in the module docstring.\n\n## Evidence\n\nObserved on change 3169 patch set 2 while landing `cb2b-7446-748c-47bc` on 2026-10-31.\nThe conflict was real and resolvable: a018 (`5cd7e2784ab`) and cb2b both inserted a new\nsection directly beneath the `docs/release-notes.md` header. Pre-rebasing and keeping both\nsections cleared it.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe conflict itself, and the adjacent-insert contention on `docs/release-notes.md` that\nproduces this class of conflict whenever two slices of one epic land close together.","id":"f6b9-8d8e-4f56-4003","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"gerrit_safe_submit.py reports every 409 as a stale revision, hiding merge conflicts"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793437281729492210,"uuid":"d2dca39f-d7fd-476b-a242-d707f270aeb3"}